sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant W as Waiter (POS UI)
    participant C as OrderController
    participant OS as OrderService
    participant RD as RecipeDeductionService
    participant IR as IngredientRepository
    participant IL as InventoryLedgerService
    participant EP as OrderEventPublisher

    W->>C: POST /api/orders (tableId, items[])
    C->>OS: submitOrder(request, waiterPrincipal)

    rect rgb(232, 245, 233)
    Note over OS,IL: Single @Transactional boundary - steps 3 to 11
    OS->>OS: tableService.openTableForOrder(tableId)
    Note right of OS: SELECT ... FOR UPDATE on table row<br/>table.status = OCCUPIED
    OS->>RD: deductForOrder(List<DeductionLine>)
    RD->>IR: findAllByIdForUpdate(sorted ingredientIds)
    Note right of IR: SELECT ... FOR UPDATE, ascending id order<br/>blocks concurrent transactions, avoids deadlock
    IR-->>RD: List<Ingredient> - all rows locked
    RD->>RD: validate stock >= required quantity
    Note right of RD: If short: InsufficientStockException<br/>HTTP 409, whole transaction rolls back
    RD->>RD: newStock = current - (qty x recipeQty)
    RD->>IR: save(ingredient)
    RD->>IL: recordRecipeDeduction(ingredient, delta, newStock)
    IL-->>RD: append-only ledger row persisted
    RD->>RD: publish ReorderThresholdBreachedEvent (if below reorder level)
    RD-->>OS: deduction complete
    OS->>OS: orderRepository.save(order) - status PENDING
    end

    Note over OS,EP: Transaction commits here - order and stock are durable
    OS->>EP: publishNewTicket(order, tableNumber)
    EP-->>W: STOMP broadcast to /topic/kitchen
    OS-->>C: OrderResponse (id, status=PENDING, items)
    C-->>W: 201 Created - order confirmed

    Note over W,EP: Alerting runs after commit: InventoryAlertService consumes the event<br/>asynchronously and drafts a Purchase Order, so a failure there can never<br/>roll back a stock deduction that already succeeded.
